> +The provider consumes only ``<linux/tdx-guest.h>``.  It does not call the TDX

The doc claims "successful replies carry the matching MR-journal boundary". The journal
(`att->log->generation`) only advances for extends that go through this CTLV instance. RTMRs are
also extendable through the native TSM-MR sysfs and the TDX misc ioctl, which this very
paragraph says remain available "independently", and those bypass the journal. So the
generation reported alongside a TDREPORT/Quote can be stale relative to the RTMR values actually
bound in the report, and the journal cannot be replayed to the reported RTMR values. Either
document the limitation or have the provider detect/resync (e.g. `mr_read` before and after).

> +misc ioctl, configfs TSM-report, or TSM-MR sysfs frontends.
