Missing 'depends on X86'/etc. is covered by `TDX_GUEST_DRIVER`, fine. But the module has no
device table/`MODULE_ALIAS` or softdep, and tdx-guest never `request_module()`s it, so with
=m nothing ever loads attestation-tdx automatically; users must modprobe by hand. Also,
the native driver supports only a single client; building another provider consumer (e.g. a
different out-of-tree client) makes this fail with `-EBUSY` at module load. Mention in help.

