Summary:
- `evidence_get`: trusts native-reported 'length' before copying into the destination blob (no
  length <= `max_length` check, uninitialised kvmalloc bounce buffer), 128 KiB bounce alloc for
  every Quote, `objects_count`==0 returns the wrong errno, unreachable else branch.
- A Quote (blocking TDVMCALL) runs under the per-instance lock, stalling all other ops.
- Doc claims the MR-journal generation matches the evidence, but native TSM-MR/ioctl extends
  bypass the journal, so it can be stale.
- Triple encoding of the MR id mapping (props, `native_mrs[]`, `mr_id-1`) plus redundant,
  unreachable bounds checks in `mr_read`/`mr_extend`/init; empty fini; duplicate structs;
  unused includes; checkpatch alignment violations; no module autoload; single-client `-EBUSY`.
